      "message": "BTW, the checkpatch reports warning for using volatile\n```\nWARNING: Use of volatile is usually wrong: see Documentation/process/volatile-considered-harmful.rst\n#115: FILE: arch/x86/kvm/pkvm/pkvm.c:1191:\n+               *(volatile typeof(shared_vcpu-\u003earch.exception) *)\u0026shared_vcpu-\u003earch.exception;\n```\nas if use proper locking, volatile is unnecessary. But our case is different and has no lock. We\u0027re using the volatile cast directly rather than field-by-field READ_ONCE, which internally use volatile casts as well. So I think we should be fine to use volatile here.",
